.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm-mr 1  "swarm 0.2.1" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm\-mr \- Merge requests: propose changes, discuss, review and merge them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm mr\fR [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Merge requests: propose changes, discuss, review and merge them
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
A repo ID or link; by default the swarm remote of this clone
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Use what is already here instead of syncing first
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
swarm\-mr\-list(1)
List open merge requests
.TP
swarm\-mr\-show(1)
Show one merge request, its commits and conversation
.TP
swarm\-mr\-create(1)
Propose a branch; run it again to add your new commits
.TP
swarm\-mr\-comment(1)
Comment on a merge request, a file in it, or another comment
.TP
swarm\-mr\-review(1)
Approve a merge request or ask for changes
.TP
swarm\-mr\-checkout(1)
Check out the proposed commits as branch mr/ID
.TP
swarm\-mr\-diff(1)
Show the proposed changes
.TP
swarm\-mr\-merge(1)
Merge into the target branch and publish (root or maintainer key)
.TP
swarm\-mr\-close(1)
Close without merging (its author or a maintainer)
.TP
swarm\-mr\-reopen(1)
Reopen a closed merge request
